+# The Daily Grind
+
+Run `pnpm install` and `pnpm start` to serve the site.
+
+Core Web Vitals monitoring loads from `/monitoring.js` and uses the self-hosted
+`web-vitals` library. CLS, INP, and LCP reports are batched for up to five seconds
+and flushed when the page becomes hidden or on `pagehide`. Empty batches are not
+sent. Failed fetch batches remain queued for the next report or lifecycle flush.
+Metrics unavailable in a browser (or INP without an interaction) are not reported.
+
+The deployment must provide a same-origin `POST /collect` handler; the development
+static server does not implement a collector. Each request is a JSON array of
+objects with `id`, `name`, `value`, `rating`, and `navigationType`. Values are
+absolute: the collector should upsert by metric `id`, replacing earlier values
+rather than summing them. LCP and INP values are milliseconds; CLS is unitless.
+Beacon delivery is best effort, and acceptance by the browser does not confirm
+server receipt.
+
+The checked-in `vendor/` assets allow static hosting without a bundler or CDN.
+After updating the pinned `web-vitals` dependency, run `pnpm vendor:web-vitals`
+and commit the refreshed assets and lockfile. The upstream Apache 2.0 license is
+included in `vendor/web-vitals.LICENSE`.
+
+Run `pnpm test` for automated batching and lifecycle tests (no browser required).
